yoloctl local patch 0004: restore process-group signals as in OpenShell v0.0.72.

OpenShell 0.1.6 routes every kill and rt_sigqueueinfo through the sandbox's
seccomp-notify broker (openshell-sandbox src/linux/process_signal.rs,
mediate_process_signal), which delivers only to one positive PID and rejects
every target <= 0 with EPERM. v0.0.72 never mediated signals, so killpg,
`kill -TERM -PGID`, kill(0) and process-group test suites failed in boxes.

A process-group kill (PID zero = the caller's own group, or -PGID other than
-1) is now delivered by the broker with kill(-PGID) unless the group is the
sandbox's own (or 0/1). The group is resolved once and the broker signals
that numeric group itself, so the caller cannot redirect it into the
sandbox's group. Broadcast kill(-1) and queued group signals
(rt_sigqueueinfo with PID <= 0) stay denied, as upstream decided. The child
filter keeps denying kill(-sandbox TGID) first (patch 0003).

Also tidies two test-only lints in patch 0003's test (no behaviour change).

